"""
One column filter, for lists that let the user filter and sort by any column.

`field` names a column the list publishes; the same names work in `sort`. Send
exactly one of the typed filters below, matching the column's type. The request
is refused as a bad request when the field is not one the list publishes, when
more than one typed filter is sent, or when the filter type does not match the
column (for example a text filter on a date column). An entry with a known
field but no filter does nothing.

Entries combine with AND, both with each other and with the list's own filter
argument, which keeps working unchanged.

Examples:
- { field: "number", text: { contains: "1042" } }
- { field: "createdAt", date: { gte: "2026-01-01T00:00:00Z" } }
"""
input ColumnFilterInput {
    "Column name the list publishes, in camelCase (createdAt). The snake_case spelling (created_at) also works."
    field: String!
    "Conditions for a text column (see StringFilter)."
    text: StringFilter
    "Conditions for a numeric column (see FloatFilter)."
    number: FloatFilter
    "Conditions for a date or timestamp column (see DateTimeFilter)."
    date: DateTimeFilter
    "Conditions for an identifier column (see IDFilter)."
    id: IDFilter
    "Conditions for a yes/no column (see BoolFilter)."
    bool: BoolFilter
}
